# ============================================================
# GPPS Procedure Attachment Snapshot Pipeline
#
# Single script, single pass -- same shape as the policy pipeline, meant
# to be handed off and re-run at any later date. Single-table version:
# aa_hsbc_gpps_gpps_procedure is the only procedure table, so there's no
# discovery loop and no per-country split -- procedures are recorded as
# GLOBAL throughout.
#
# In ONE pass per procedure (compute its audit row, then immediately
# copy its matched files):
#
#   1. AUDIT -- compares what the BQ/JSON record says should exist
#      (active procedureApplication.appendix[]/guidance[] items,
#      actvFlg == "Y", matched on docName) against what's actually
#      sitting in the source GCS bucket.
#   2. COPY -- for every matched attachment, copies it from the source
#      bucket into this run's own timestamped snapshot folder.
#   3. LOG -- writes a diagnostics log directly into that snapshot
#      folder in GCS, alongside the files it describes.
#
# Source (READ-ONLY): gpps-11910707-conformed-prod, via py_gcs_tools.GCSClient
#   -- only list_objects() / download_object() ever called against it.
#   Never any write/upload/delete call against this bucket.
#
# Destination (WRITE): cmlp_exp_003_1_prod, via google.cloud.storage
#   gs://cmlp_exp_003_1_prod/MODEL_2/gpps_attachments/procedures_{timestamp}/
#   global/{procedure_id}/{filename}
#   -- "global" is a fixed folder name (procedures have no country split),
#      parallel to how the policy pipeline's Global table ("aa") maps to
#      the "global" folder there.
#   -- Flat under procedure_id, no version subfolder: only the latest
#      version's attachments are kept; re-running overwrites with the
#      then-current latest.
#
# UNVERIFIED ASSUMPTION carried over from earlier procedure scripts: the
# SOURCE prefix "gpps_attachment/procedure/{id}/{version}/" (singular
# "procedure") has never been independently confirmed against a live
# bucket listing, the way the policy prefix was (manually, against a
# screenshot). Run the SECTION 0 sanity check below on one procedure with
# known attachments before trusting a full run -- if that prefix is
# wrong, every procedure will silently show 0 matches rather than erroring.
#
# Version selection: per procedure_core_id, the row with
# versn.procVersnStatCde == "PUBL" and the highest version_num (procedures
# use a different status field name than policies, per the earlier wiki
# cross-reference); falls back to the highest version_num overall if no
# PUBL version exists.
#
# Output:
#   - Local: GPPS_Procedure_Attachment_Snapshot.xlsx, three sheets --
#     Audit (one row per procedure), Overall level (same Set A/Set B
#     rollup as the policy pipeline, naturally collapsing to one row
#     since there's no country split here), Set B - missing procedures.
#   - GCS: diagnostics_log.txt written directly into this run's snapshot
#     folder.
# ============================================================

